<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
<p>Data Informatics &amp; Technologies B.V. (DataiTECH) is the controller for the personal data described in this statement, as defined in the General Data Protection Regulation (AVG/GDPR).</p>
<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>When you email us:</strong> your name, email address, organisation and anything you choose to include in your message.</li>
<li><strong>When you visit the website:</strong> our web server processes technical data such as your IP address and browser type, which is needed to deliver the page securely.</li>
</ul>
<p>This website does not use cookies, analytics or tracking. Fonts are hosted on our own server, so your visit is not shared with third parties such as Google.</p>
<h2>Why we use it</h2>
<ul>
<li>To answer your question and follow up on a possible collaboration (legitimate interest, or steps before entering into a contract).</li>
<li>To keep the website secure and available (legitimate interest).</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your data and do not use it for automated decision-making.</p>
<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>We keep correspondence for as long as needed to handle your question and any resulting collaboration, and no longer than legally required or allowed. Server logs are kept for a limited period for security purposes.</p>
<h2>Who we share it with</h2>
<p>Only with service providers that help us run our email and website, under a data processing agreement, and with authorities when the law requires it.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You have the right to access, correct or delete your personal data, to restrict or object to its use, and to data portability. Email us at <a href="mailto:info@dataitech.eu">info@dataitech.eu</a> to make a request. We respond within one month.</p>
<p>If you are not satisfied with how we handle your data, you can file a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection Authority, the <a href="https://autoriteitpersoonsgegevens.nl" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens</a>.</p>
      </article>
